UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="wpb_wrapper"><h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Shape Young Futures With a Diploma of Early Childhood Education and Care</strong></h1> <p>Choosing a career that shapes young minds is more than a professional decision—it’s a purpose-driven path. <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/">Skyline International College</a> offers a future-focused learning experience through the Diploma of Early Childhood Education and Care, designed for individuals who want to build meaningful, long-term careers in Australia’s growing education sector. This nationally recognised qualification equips students with practical skills, theoretical knowledge, and real-world experience needed to thrive in regulated early learning environments.</p> <section class="mbr-section courses-section"> <div class="lw_col-inner"> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Why Early Childhood Education Is a Career With Purpose</strong></h2> <p>Early childhood educators play a vital role during the most critical years of a child’s development. This qualification prepares learners to confidently guide children’s learning, well-being, and social development while meeting national regulatory standards.</p> <h3><strong>What Makes This Qualification Valuable?</strong></h3> <ul class="catpara"> <li><strong>High industry demand –</strong> Early childhood educators are consistently sought after across Australia.</li> <li><strong>Career progression opportunities –</strong> Pathways into leadership, coordination, or further study</li> <li><strong>Hands-on learning –</strong> Real workplace exposure builds confidence and job readiness</li> <li><strong>National recognition –</strong> Approved under Australian education and care frameworks</li> </ul> <p>This makes the diploma of early childhood education and care across Sydney an ideal choice for students seeking stability, growth, and meaningful work.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>CHC50125 Diploma of Early Childhood Education and Care</strong></h2> <p>This qualification reflects the role of educators in early childhood education and care who work in regulated children’s education and care services in Australia. Educators at this level are responsible for designing and implementing curriculum that meets the requirements of an approved learning framework and for maintaining compliance in other areas of service operations. They use specialised knowledge and analyse and apply theoretical concepts to diverse work situations. They may have responsibility for the supervision of volunteers or other educators.</p> <p>Early childhood educators work in long day care centres, family day care, pre-schools or kindergartens. To achieve this qualification, the individual must have completed a total of at least 280 hours of work in a regulated children’s education and care service in Australia as detailed in the Assessment Requirements of units of competency. The total number of hours may be applied collectively across all units of competency that include the requirement for workplace hours.</p> <p>No occupational licensing, certification or specific legislative requirements apply to this qualification at the time of publication.</p> <p>Under the Education and Care Services National Law (2011) the Australian Children’s Education and Care Quality Authority (ACECQA) publishes lists of approved early childhood education and care qualifications and information regarding regulatory requirements here: <a data-wpel-link="external" href="http://www.acecqa.gov.au" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" target="_blank">www.acecqa.gov.au</a>.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Who This Course Is For</strong></h2> <p>The individual support course is tailored for:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Individuals who want to work as aged care or home care assistants</li> <li>People re-entering the workforce are looking for a reliable, growing industry</li> <li>International students seeking a CRICOS-registered qualification</li> <li>Anyone who values person-centred care and wants a career that makes a difference</li> </ul> <p><img alt="Course Image" class="title-img" decoding="async" src="https://sic.edu.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/childhood-care2-300x195.jpg"/></p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>What You’ll Learn During the Course</strong></h2> <p>This course blends theory with practice to ensure graduates are workplace-ready.</p> <h3>Important Learning Areas Include:</h3> <ul class="catpara"> <li><strong>Child development &amp; wellbeing –</strong> Supporting emotional, physical, and cognitive growth</li> <li><strong>Curriculum planning –</strong> Implementing approved learning frameworks</li> <li><strong>Health, safety &amp; compliance –</strong> Maintaining safe and regulated learning environments</li> <li><strong>Professional leadership –</strong> Supervising staff and collaborating with families</li> </ul> <p>Through structured training and workplace hours, students gain the confidence to succeed in diverse early learning settings.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Who Should Enrol in This Course?</strong></h2> <p>The diploma of early childhood education and care across Sydney is ideal for:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Individuals passionate about working with children</li> <li>Students seeking PR-aligned education pathways</li> <li>Educators wanting to upskill or move into leadership roles</li> <li>Career changers looking for meaningful, people-focused work</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Career Outcomes After Completion</strong></h2> <p>Graduates of this qualification can pursue roles such as:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Early Childhood Educator</li> <li>Lead Educator</li> <li>Room Leader</li> <li>Childcare Centre Supervisor</li> </ul> <p>The diploma of early childhood education and care opens doors to long-term career stability within Australia’s regulated education sector.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Start Your Journey With Confidence</strong></h2> <p>A rewarding career begins with the proper education and support. This qualification offers the skills, experience, and recognition needed to succeed in early childhood education.</p> <p><a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/contact/">Enquire today</a> to learn more, speak with our <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/admissions-skyline-international-college/">admissions team</a>, or begin your enrolment journey now. Your future as a qualified early childhood educator starts here at Skyline International College. You can get more courses from us, along with this, such as <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/course/chc33021-certificate-iii-in-individual-support-ageing/">individual support</a>, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/course/chc52021-diploma-of-community-services/">community services</a>, and <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/hospitality-courses/">hospitality courses</a>.</p> </div> </section> </div>',
    total_course_duration = '52 Weeks(Includes term breaks)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 14000,
    enrolment_fee = 200,
    materials_fee = 2000,
    entry_requirements = '<div aria-expanded="true" class="w-tabs-section-content" id="content-1645787573297-1de0d9ea-2159" style=""><div class="w-tabs-section-content-h i-cf"><div class="wpb_text_column taab active"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><p>Skyline International College (SIC) follows the Community Services Training Package guidance for the entry requirements for this qualification. Entry to this qualification is open to individuals who:</p> <ul> <li>hold a CHC30125 Certificate III in Early Childhood Education and Care or equivalent.</li> </ul> <h4>Academic Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li>Minimum completion of Australian Year 12 secondary school education equivalent or above.</li> </ul> <h4>English Language Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify;"><span class="agcmg">Academic IELTS 6.0 overall, with no less than 5.5 in each band or Upper Intermediate or EAP completion from an approved ELICOS/ESL centre Or Equivalent English Test (e.g. PTE, TOEFL).</span></p> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify; color: rgba(35,31,32,var(--o42jjq,1)); caret-color: #231f20; --8sd0kg: none; --cyv3zq: 12px; --gjplxq: 1.985; --s8nbea: p;"><span style="color: rgba(35,31,32,var(--o42jjq,1)); caret-color: #231f20; --ys-xuq: none; font-kerning: none;"><span class="agcmg">An AQF qualification at Certificate III level or above in any discipline,</span> delivered and assessed in English, will also satisfy both academic and</span> English requirements.</p> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify;"><span class="agcmg">Successfully complete the Language, Literacy, and Numeracy (LLN) and Digital literacy assessment provided by SIC prior to finalization of enrolment.</span></p> </li> </ul> <h4>Physical requirements:</h4> <ul> <li>Participants of this course should have a certain level of fitness as it involves tasks like lifting children, cleaning, mopping, and rearranging furniture. Participants should be prepared for these manual handling responsibilities that are integral to the job.</li> </ul> </div></div></div></div>',
