UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="wpb_wrapper"><h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Become a Leader in Community Services | Study Across Sydney With Confidence</strong></h1> <p>If you’re ready to build a career that improves lives and strengthens communities, the Diploma of Community Services at <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/">Skyline International College</a> is the right place to begin. This nationally recognised qualification is ideal for people who want to work on the frontline of social change, supporting individuals, families, and communities through complex challenges.</p> <p>At Skyline, we combine career-focused learning with personal support, helping you grow into a confident, capable professional. As one of the most trusted providers of community services courses across Sydney, our focus is always on practical, real-world training that prepares you for jobs that matter.</p> <section class="mbr-section courses-section"> <div class="lw_col-inner"> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Who Is This Course For?</strong></h2> <p>This qualification is perfect for anyone who:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Wants to step into a leadership or case management role in the community sector</li> <li>Is currently working in social services and looking to upskill</li> <li>Seeks a meaningful, purpose-driven career</li> <li>Is an international student wanting a CRICOS-accredited pathway in Australia</li> </ul> <p>Whether your passion lies in youth services, mental health, disability support, family care, or program coordination, this course gives you the tools and confidence to lead change.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>CHC52025 Diploma of Community Services</strong></h2> <p>This qualification reflects the role of community services workers involved in the delivery, management and coordination of person-centred services to individuals, groups, and communities. At this level, workers have specialised skills in community services and work autonomously within their scope of practice under broad directions from senior management.</p> <p>Workers support people to make changes in their lives to improve personal and social wellbeing, and may also have responsibility for the supervision of other workers and volunteers. They may also undertake case management and program coordination.</p> <p>To achieve this qualification, the candidate must have completed at least 200 hours of work as detailed in the Assessment Requirements of units of competency. The skills in this qualification must be applied in accordance with Commonwealth and State or Territory legislation, Australian standards and industry codes of practice.</p> <p>No occupational licensing, certification or specific legislative requirements apply to this qualification at the time of publication.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Course Overview | Learn to Guide, Manage and Support</strong></h2> <p>The diploma of community services equips you with specialised knowledge and practical abilities to work autonomously, lead teams, and manage support programs. You’ll learn how to:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Plan and coordinate person-centred services</li> <li>Provide case management and advocacy</li> <li>Lead community engagement initiatives</li> <li>Understand legal, ethical, and professional standards</li> <li>Supervise staff and volunteers effectively</li> </ul> <p>A key feature of this course is a 200-hour mandatory work placement, which gives you on-the-ground experience in real community service settings. It’s not just about gaining knowledge; it’s about knowing how to apply it in a way that makes a real impact.</p> <p><img alt="Course Image" class="title-img" decoding="async" src="https://sic.edu.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Living-in-Sydney.jpg"/></p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Career Opportunities and Pathways</strong></h2> <p>This qualification opens up a wide range of roles in government, non-profit, and private sectors. Possible job titles include:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Case Manager</li> <li>Program Coordinator</li> <li>Family Services Officer</li> <li>Community Worker</li> <li>Youth Worker</li> <li>Support Services Manager</li> </ul> <p>With the increasing demand for experienced professionals in this space, completing this course places you in a strong position for employment and career progression. The training also sets a strong foundation if you choose to continue into higher-level qualifications later.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Why Train With Skyline International College?</strong></h2> <p>Skyline International College is known for delivering career-ready education in a supportive, student-focused environment. Our community services courses across Sydney are led by industry professionals who bring years of real experience into the classroom.</p> <p>We offer:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Small classes for personalised attention</li> <li>Trainers who are active professionals in the sector</li> <li>Practical placement support through industry partnerships</li> <li>A modern campus located near Sydney with accessible transport links</li> </ul> <p>At Skyline International College, you’re not just another student; you’re a future community leader. Get more courses with us, such as <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc30220-certificate-iii-in-carpentry/">carpentry</a>, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/hospitality-courses/">hospitality</a>, and <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/automotive-courses/">automotive courses</a> across Sydney.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Ready to Take the Next Step?</strong></h2> <p>If you’re serious about making a long-term difference and want to gain recognised qualifications, the Diploma of Community Services at Skyline International College is your ideal starting point.</p> <p><a data-wpel-link="external" href="https://sic.rtomanager.com.au/Publics/PublicsPages/StudentApply/pp_Application_Step0.aspx" rel="nofollow external noopener noreferrer">Apply now</a> or speak to our <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/admissions-skyline-international-college/">admissions team</a> to find out more about enrolment, fees, and placement opportunities. Your future in community services starts here. <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/contact/">Contact us</a>!</p> </div> </section> </div>',
    total_course_duration = '104 Weeks(Includes term breaks)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 21000,
    enrolment_fee = 200,
    materials_fee = 4000,
    entry_requirements = '<div aria-expanded="true" class="w-tabs-section-content" id="content-1645787573297-1de0d9ea-2159" style=""><div class="w-tabs-section-content-h i-cf"><div class="wpb_text_column taab active"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><p>Skyline International College (SIC) follows the Community Services Training Package guidance for the entry requirements for this qualification. There are no entry requirements for this qualification and direct entry is accepted.</p> <h4>Academic Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li>Minimum completion of Australian Year 12 secondary school education equivalent or above.</li> </ul> <h4>English Language Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify;"><span class="agcmg">Academic IELTS 6.0 overall, with no less than 5.5 in each band or Upper Intermediate or EAP completion from an approved ELICOS/ESL centre Or Equivalent English Test (e.g. PTE, TOEFL).</span></p> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify; color: rgba(35,31,32,var(--o42jjq,1)); caret-color: #231f20; --8sd0kg: none; --cyv3zq: 12px; --gjplxq: 1.985; --s8nbea: p;"><span style="color: rgba(35,31,32,var(--o42jjq,1)); caret-color: #231f20; --ys-xuq: none; font-kerning: none;"><span class="agcmg">An AQF qualification at Certificate III level or above in any discipline,</span> delivered and assessed in English, will also satisfy both academic and</span> English requirements.</p> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify;"><span class="agcmg">Successfully complete the Language, Literacy, and Numeracy (LLN) and Digital literacy assessment provided by SIC prior to finalization of enrolment.</span></p> </li> </ul> <h4>Physical requirements:</h4> <ul> <li>Participants of this course should have reasonable level of fitness as the role may involve a variety of manual handling tasks that require physical activity, such as bending, lifting and standing for long periods of time.</li> </ul> </div></div></div></div>',
