UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="wpb_wrapper"><h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Get Skilled, Get Hired | Certificate III in Carpentry at Skyline International College</strong></h1> <p>If you’re looking to build a practical, hands-on career in construction, the Certificate III in Carpentry at Skyline International College gives you the skills and qualifications employers value. This nationally recognised course is tailored for students who want to work as carpenters across residential and commercial job sites in Australia. Whether you’re starting fresh, upskilling, or formalising your existing experience, this program prepares you to work confidently with timber, tools, and construction systems, while staying compliant with industry standards.</p> <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The CPC30220 Certificate III in Carpentry focuses on developing practical trade skills, workplace safety knowledge, and industry-standard work practices required for residential and commercial construction environments.</span></p> <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Students enrolled in this qualification may also have the opportunity to participate in Skyline International College’s optional Carpentry Job Ready Program. This separate non-accredited program is designed to help learners further develop workplace confidence, practical trade techniques, employability skills, and industry awareness through additional training and mentoring by experienced industry professionals.</span></p> <section class="mbr-section courses-section"> <div class="lw_col-inner"> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>CPC30220 Certificate III in Carpentry</strong></h2> <p>This is a trade qualification for carpenters in residential and commercial workplaces. It includes setting out, manufacturing, constructing, assembling, installing and repairing products made using timber and non-timber materials. State and territory jurisdictions may have different licensing, legislative, regulatory or certification requirements. Relevant state and territory regulatory authorities should be consulted to confirm those requirements. Completion of the general construction induction training program, specified in the Safe Work Australia model Code of Practice: Construction Work, is required by anyone carrying out construction work. Achievement of CPCCWHS1001 Prepare to work safely in the construction industry meets this requirement.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>What This Course Offers</strong></h2> <p>Skyline’s training is structured to match real-world expectations. You’ll be taught by trainers with on-site experience and learn in simulated workshop environments to build capability before entering a live job site. This carpentry course covers essential trade skills, including:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Reading and interpreting plans</li> <li>Framing for floors, walls, and roofs</li> <li>Installation of doors, windows, and stair components</li> <li>Use of power tools and equipment</li> <li>Construction of structures using timber and alternative materials</li> <li>Workplace health and safety practices</li> </ul> <p>As a job-ready program in Carpentry, the training combines classroom learning with hands-on workshop experience to ensure students develop skills that align with current industry requirements.</p> <p>The course also includes general construction induction training (CPCCWHS1001), which is required before you can legally work on any construction site in Australia. Completing this unit qualifies you to apply for a White Card. <img alt="Course Image" class="title-img" decoding="async" src="https://sic.edu.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Graduate-Diploma-of-Learning-Management-1.jpg"/></p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Who Is This Course For?</strong></h2> <p>This course is ideal for:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>School leavers ready to join the trades</li> <li>Labourers wanting formal training for better job opportunities</li> <li>International students seeking CRICOS-accredited carpentry courses</li> <li>People who enjoy physical, hands-on work and want to build something that lasts</li> </ul> <p>There’s no better time to train; Australia’s construction sector continues to grow, creating steady demand for skilled tradespeople.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Career Outcomes You Can Expect</strong></h2> <p>With a Certificate III in Carpentry, you’ll be equipped for roles such as:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Apprentice Carpenter</li> <li>Construction Site Assistant</li> <li>Framing and Fixing Carpenter</li> <li>Domestic or Commercial Carpentry Worker</li> </ul> <p>After gaining industry experience, you may also choose to become a licensed builder or start your own contracting business. This qualification lays the groundwork for long-term growth in the building and construction industry. Get more courses from us, such as <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/hospitality-courses/">hospitality</a>, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/automotive-courses/">car mechanic</a>, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/community-services/">community service</a> and <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/course/chc30121-certificate-iii-in-early-childhood-education-and-care/">childcare</a>.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Why Choose Skyline International College</strong></h2> <p><a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/">Skyline International College</a> is a respected name among vocational training providers across Sydney. We offer a learning experience that’s career-focused, practical, and supportive. Here’s what makes us different:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Small classes led by industry-trained professionals</li> <li>Hands-on training using fundamental tools and materials</li> <li>Guidance for construction site placement and safety readiness</li> <li>Clear, structured pathways for both domestic and international students</li> <li>Sydney-based campus with access to public transport</li> </ul> <p>As a CRICOS-registered provider, we welcome international students looking to start or advance their careers in Australia.</p> <p>If you’re searching for a job-ready program in Carpentry that combines recognised qualifications with hands-on industry training, Skyline International College provides a strong pathway into the construction sector.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Ready to Start Building Your Career?</strong></h2> <p>If you’re ready to turn your skills into a professional qualification, the Certificate III in Carpentry at Skyline International College offers the support, structure, and hands-on training you need to succeed. <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/contact/">Contact us</a> to get more details from our <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/admissions-skyline-international-college/">admissions team</a> today to check your eligibility and secure your place in our next intake. Your future as a qualified carpenter starts now.</p> </div> </section> </div>',
    total_course_duration = '104 Weeks(Includes term breaks)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 40000,
    enrolment_fee = 200,
    materials_fee = 2000,
    entry_requirements = '<div aria-expanded="true" class="w-tabs-section-content" id="content-1645787573297-1de0d9ea-2159" style=""><div class="w-tabs-section-content-h i-cf"><div class="wpb_text_column taab active"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><p>Skyline International College (SIC) follows the CPC Construction, Plumbing and Services Training Package guidance for the entry requirements for this qualification. There are no entry requirements for this qualification and direct entry is accepted.</p> <h4>Academic Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li>Minimum completion of Australian Year 12 secondary school education equivalent or above.</li> </ul> <h4>English Language Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify;"><span class="agcmg">Academic IELTS 6.0 overall, with no less than 5.5 in each band or Upper Intermediate or EAP completion from an approved ELICOS/ESL centre Or Equivalent English Test (e.g. PTE, TOEFL).</span></p> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify; color: rgba(35,31,32,var(--o42jjq,1)); caret-color: #231f20; --8sd0kg: none; --cyv3zq: 12px; --gjplxq: 1.985; --s8nbea: p;"><span style="color: rgba(35,31,32,var(--o42jjq,1)); caret-color: #231f20; --ys-xuq: none; font-kerning: none;"><span class="agcmg">An AQF qualification at Certificate III level or above in any discipline,</span> delivered and assessed in English, will also satisfy both academic and</span> English requirements.</p> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify;"><span class="agcmg">Successfully complete the Language, Literacy, and Numeracy (LLN) and Digital literacy assessment provided by SIC prior to finalization of enrolment.</span></p> </li> </ul> <h4>Physical requirements:</h4> <ul> <li>Participants of this course must have the ability to carry out workshop training involving physical activity, including lifting. A desire to work in a variety of indoor and outdoor environments is a key to work as a carpenter.</li> </ul> </div></div></div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc30220-certificate-iii-in-carpentry/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '116681F';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="wpb_wrapper"><h1>Build a Colourful Career with a Painting and Decorating Course in Sydney</h1> <p>A skilled trade can offer more than just a job; it can provide long-term career stability, practical skills, and opportunities to work on exciting projects. For those who enjoy hands-on work and transforming spaces, painting and decorating can be a rewarding career choice.</p> <p><a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/">Skyline International College</a> offers a comprehensive painting and decorating course in Sydney that helps students develop industry-ready skills through practical training and expert guidance. Whether you are starting your career or looking to gain a recognised qualification, our programs are designed to prepare you for success in the construction and renovation industry.</p> <h2><strong>Create Spaces That Inspire</strong></h2> <p>Painting and decorating is about much more than applying colour to walls. It is a skilled trade that transforms homes, offices, retail stores, and commercial buildings into attractive and functional spaces.</p> <p>Our Certificate 3 in Painting and Decorating provides practical training that helps students develop the confidence and technical expertise required by today’s employers. Delivered by experienced trainers, the course focuses on industry-relevant techniques, workplace safety, surface preparation, decorative finishes, and professional painting methods.</p> <p>As a registered training provider, we are committed to helping students gain valuable skills that can open doors to long-term career opportunities.</p> <h2><strong>Why Choose Skyline International College?</strong></h2> <p>Learning from experienced professionals makes a significant difference in your career journey. Our trainers bring real industry knowledge into every lesson, ensuring students learn techniques that are used on actual worksites.</p> <h3>What Makes Us Different?</h3> <ul> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Industry-experienced trainers</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Practical, hands-on learning environment</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Supportive learning atmosphere</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Flexible study pathways</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Modern training facilities</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Career-focused curriculum</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Affordable course fees and excellent value</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Support for international students</li> </ul> <p>We believe quality education should be accessible. That is why our training programs are competitively priced while maintaining high educational standards.</p> <h2><strong>What You Will Learn</strong></h2> <p>The painting and decorating course in Sydney covers a wide range of skills needed to succeed in the industry.</p> <h3>Key Areas of Training</h3> <ul> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Surface preparation techniques</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Colour matching and selection</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Application of paints and coatings</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Decorative finishes</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Wallpaper installation</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Spray-painting methods</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Workplace safety procedures</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Tools and equipment handling</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Estimating materials and project planning</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Industry compliance requirements</li> </ul> <p>Through practical workshops and guided learning, students gain valuable experience that can be applied directly on construction and renovation projects.</p> <h3>Course Snapshot</h3> <ul> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Qualification</strong>: Certificate III in Painting and Decorating.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Learning Style</strong>: A combination of practical, hands-on training and classroom-based learning.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Trainers</strong>: Learn from industry-experienced professionals with extensive trade knowledge.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Student Support</strong>: Access academic assistance and career guidance throughout your studies.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Training Focus</strong>: Develop real workplace skills that align with current industry standards and employer expectations.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Career Outcome</strong>: Graduate with the skills and qualifications needed to work as a Painting and Decorating professional.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Suitable For</strong>: Designed for both local and international students seeking a career in the painting and decorating industry.</li> </ul> <p>This structured approach ensures students graduate with the knowledge and confidence employers are looking for.</p> <h2><strong>Turn Skills into Career Opportunities</strong></h2> <p>The construction and renovation industries continue to create demand for qualified painters and decorators. Employers value workers who have practical experience, recognised qualifications, and an understanding of industry standards.</p> <p>Completing the Certificate 3 in Painting and Decorating can help you access a range of career opportunities while building a foundation for future growth.</p> <h3>Potential Career Outcomes</h3> <ul> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Residential Painter</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Commercial Painter</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Decorative Finisher</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Maintenance Painter</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Painting Contractor</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Surface Preparation Specialist</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Construction Industry Worker</li> </ul> <h2><strong>Learn from Trainers Who Have Been There</strong></h2> <p>The quality of training often depends on who teaches it. Our trainers have real industry experience and understand what employers expect from today’s tradies.</p> <p>Instead of focusing only on textbooks, students learn practical methods, workplace techniques, and professional standards that are relevant to current industry needs. This hands-on approach at Skyline International College helps learners become more confident and job-ready.</p> <p>As a college regulated by ASQA and registered on CRICOS, we provide training that meets recognised Australian education standards.</p> <h2><strong>Quality Training at Competitive Prices</strong></h2> <p>Investing in education should not mean overpaying. Skyline International College is committed to providing quality training at competitive fees, making professional education more accessible for students.</p> <p>Our courses are designed to deliver real value through practical learning, industry-focused training, experienced educators, and ongoing student support.</p> <p>Students often choose us because they receive high-quality education without the premium price tag often associated with vocational training. Our painting and decorating course in Sydney offers an excellent balance between affordability and career-focused learning.</p> <h2><strong>The Benefits of Studying with Us</strong></h2> <p>Choosing the right college can have a significant impact on your future career.</p> <h3>Benefits You Can Expect</h3> <ul> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Gain practical, hands-on industry skills</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Learn from experienced trainers</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Receive a nationally-recognised qualification</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Improve your employment opportunities</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Build confidence in real workplace environments</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Access support throughout your studies</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Study in a welcoming environment for international students</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Enjoy competitive course pricing and excellent value</li> </ul> <h2><strong>Your Future Starts with the Right Qualification</strong></h2> <p>Every successful career begins with the right training. Whether you are entering the workforce for the first time, changing careers, or looking to formalise your skills, our programs are designed to help you achieve your goals. Get more certified courses with us, such as <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc30220-certificate-iii-in-carpentry/">carpentry courses</a>, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/automotive-courses/">car mechanic courses</a>, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc33020-certificate-iii-in-bricklaying-and-blocklaying/">bricklaying courses</a>, and an <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/information-technology-courses/">IT job-ready program in Sydney</a>.</p> <p>The Certificate 3 in Painting and Decorating provides the practical knowledge, industry exposure, and recognised qualification needed to build a successful future in the trade.</p> <h2><strong>Enrol Today</strong></h2> <p><a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/contact/">Contact our team today</a> to learn more about course intakes, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/admissions-skyline-international-college/">eligibility requirements</a>, fees, and enrolment options. Let us help you develop the skills, confidence, and qualifications needed to create a brighter future in the painting and decorating industry.</p> </div>',
    total_course_duration = '52 Weeks (Includes term breaks)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 28000,
    enrolment_fee = 200,
    materials_fee = 2000,
    entry_requirements = '<div aria-expanded="true" class="w-tabs-section-content" id="content-1645787573297-1de0d9ea-2159" style=""><div class="w-tabs-section-content-h i-cf"><div class="wpb_text_column taab active"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><p>Skyline International College (SIC) follows the CPC Construction, Plumbing and Services Training Package guidance for the entry requirements for this qualification. There are no entry requirements for this qualification and direct entry is accepted.</p> <h4>Age and Academic Requirements:</h4> <p>International students must be 17 years or older and minimum completion of Australian Year 12 secondary school education equivalent or above.</p> <h4>English Language Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li>Academic IELTS 6.0 overall, no less than 5.5 in each band, upper intermediate, or EAP from an approved ELICOS/ESL center.</li> <li>Any AQF qualification at the Certificate III level or above in any discipline area delivered and assessed in English only will be deemed as meeting both the academic and English language entry requirements.</li> <li>Successfully complete the Language, Literacy, and Numeracy (LLN) and Digital literacy assessment provided by SIC prior to finalization of enrolment.</li> </ul> <h4>Physical requirements:</h4> <p>Participants of this course must have the ability to carry out workshop training involving physical activity, including lifting. A desire to work in a variety of indoor and outdoor environments is a key to work as a painter and Decorator.</p> </div></div></div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc30620-certificate-iii-in-painting-and-decorating/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '120609B';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="wpb_wrapper"><h1><strong>CPC31320 Certificate III in Wall and Floor Tiling</strong></h1> <p>This qualification provides a trade outcome in wall and floor tiling for residential and commercial construction work. The qualification has core unit of competency requirements that cover common skills for the construction industry, as well as the specialist field of work, wall and floor tiling. Tilers work with materials like ceramic, glass, slate, marble and clay. They cut these materials and lay tiles on walls and floors, both interior and exterior. They may also add decorative touches to their basic work.<br/> State and territory jurisdictions may have different licensing, legislative, regulatory or certification requirements. Relevant state and territory regulatory authorities should be consulted to confirm those requirements.<br/> This qualification is suitable for an Australian apprenticeship pathway.<br/> Completion of the general construction induction training program, specified in the Safe Work Australia model Code of Practice: Construction Work, is required by anyone carrying out construction work. Achievement of CPCCWHS1001 Prepare to work safely in the construction industry meets this requirement.</p> </div>',
    total_course_duration = '104 Weeks(Includes term breaks)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 40000,
    enrolment_fee = 200,
    materials_fee = 2000,
    entry_requirements = '<div aria-expanded="true" class="w-tabs-section-content" id="content-1645787573297-1de0d9ea-2159" style=""><div class="w-tabs-section-content-h i-cf"><div class="wpb_text_column taab active"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><p>Skyline International College (SIC) follows the CPC Construction, Plumbing and Services Training Package guidance for the entry requirements for this qualification. There are no entry requirements for this qualification and direct entry is accepted.</p> <h4>Academic Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li>Minimum completion of Australian Year 12 secondary school education equivalent or above.</li> </ul> <h4>English Language Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify;"><span class="agcmg">Academic IELTS 6.0 overall, with no less than 5.5 in each band or Upper Intermediate or EAP completion from an approved ELICOS/ESL centre Or Equivalent English Test (e.g. PTE, TOEFL).</span></p> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify; color: rgba(35,31,32,var(--o42jjq,1)); caret-color: #231f20; --8sd0kg: none; --cyv3zq: 12px; --gjplxq: 1.985; --s8nbea: p;"><span style="color: rgba(35,31,32,var(--o42jjq,1)); caret-color: #231f20; --ys-xuq: none; font-kerning: none;"><span class="agcmg">An AQF qualification at Certificate III level or above in any discipline,</span> delivered and assessed in English, will also satisfy both academic and</span> English requirements.</p> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify;"><span class="agcmg">Successfully complete the Language, Literacy, and Numeracy (LLN) and Digital literacy assessment provided by SIC prior to finalization of enrolment.</span></p> </li> </ul> <h4>Physical requirements</h4> <ul> <li>Participants of this course should have a good level of fitness to manage the physical demands of the job, including lifting boxes of tiles and adhesive bags, crouching, kneeling and bending to perform work.</li> </ul> </div></div></div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc31320-certificate-iii-in-wall-and-floor-tiling/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '116680G';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="wpb_wrapper"><h1>Enrol in an Australian Professional Bricklaying Course in Sydney</h1> <p><a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/">Skyline International College</a> helps students gain industry-ready skills through a bricklaying course in Sydney designed for both local and international learners. Our college combines practical training with professional knowledge, helping students develop the confidence and expertise needed to enter the construction sector. With experienced trainers, modern learning facilities, and recognised training standards, we help students take the first step toward a rewarding career.</p> <h2><strong>Turn Hands-On Skills into Real Career Opportunities</strong></h2> <p>Bricklaying is one of the most important trades in the construction industry. From residential homes and commercial buildings to large infrastructure projects, skilled bricklayers play a vital role in shaping Australia’s built environment.</p> <p>Our training focuses on practical learning and industry-relevant techniques. Students gain the skills needed to work safely, efficiently, and professionally on construction sites while developing a strong understanding of building materials, tools, and construction methods.</p> <h3>What You Can Learn</h3> <p>Our course may cover a range of essential skills, including:</p> <ul> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Reading and interpreting construction plans</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Brick and block laying techniques</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Mortar preparation and application</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Construction measurements and calculations</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Workplace health and safety practices</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Use and maintenance of bricklaying tools</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Building walls, arches, and structural components</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Working effectively within construction teams</li> </ul> <h2><strong>Benefits of Studying a Bricklaying Course</strong></h2> <p>The construction sector continues to offer strong employment opportunities across Australia. Completing a bricklaying course in Sydney can open doors to various career pathways and long-term growth opportunities.</p> <h3>Key Benefits Include:</h3> <ul> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">High demand for skilled tradies</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Practical, hands-on career path</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Opportunities to work on diverse projects</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Potential for career advancement</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Development of valuable trade skills</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Ability to work across different construction sectors</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Strong earning potential with experience</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;">Pathways to further training and qualifications</li> </ul> <p>For students who enjoy working with their hands and seeing tangible results from their efforts, bricklaying can be a highly rewarding profession.</p> <h2><strong>Your Learning Journey at a Glance</strong></h2> <p>Throughout the course, you will progressively develop the knowledge and practical skills needed to succeed in the construction industry, including:</p> <ul> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Construction Fundamentals</strong> – Gain a strong understanding of building processes, construction methods, and commonly used materials.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Practical Bricklaying Skills</strong> – Develop hands-on experience using industry-standard bricklaying techniques and tools.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Safety Training</strong> – Learn essential workplace health and safety practices to help maintain a safe and compliant work environment.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Project Work</strong> – Apply your knowledge in practical projects that reflect real-world construction scenarios.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Industry Knowledge</strong> – Build an understanding of construction standards, industry expectations, and professional work practices.</li> <li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Career Preparation</strong> – Develop practical skills and workplace readiness that support future employment opportunities in the construction sector.</li> </ul> <p>This structured learning approach helps students build confidence, strengthen their practical abilities, and prepare for the day-to-day realities of working in the construction industry.</p> <h2><strong>Simple Admission Process</strong></h2> <p>Starting your education journey should be straightforward. At Skyline International College, we have designed a simple admission process to help students enrol with ease.</p> <h3>How to Apply</h3> <h4>Step 1: Enquiry</h4> <p>Contact our team to discuss your course options and eligibility requirements.</p> <h4>Step 2: Submit Your Application</h4> <p>Complete the application form and provide the necessary supporting documents.</p> <h4>Step 3: Application Assessment</h4> <p>Our admissions team reviews your application and confirms your eligibility.</p> <h4>Step 4: Receive Your Offer</h4> <p>Successful applicants receive an offer letter with enrolment details.</p> <h4>Step 5: Confirm Your Enrolment</h4> <p>Accept the offer and complete the required enrolment procedures.</p> <h4>Step 6: Begin Your Studies</h4> <p>Start your learning journey and work towards a successful career in construction.</p> <p>Our team provides support throughout the process to ensure a smooth transition into student life.</p> <h2><strong>A Learning Environment Designed for Success</strong></h2> <p>Education is about more than gaining qualifications. It is about building confidence, developing practical abilities, and preparing for future opportunities. Skyline International College welcomes students from diverse backgrounds and provides an environment where learning is engaging, supportive, and career-focused. Explore our <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc30220-certificate-iii-in-carpentry/">carpentry courses</a>, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc50220-diploma-of-building-and-construction-building/">construction management courses</a>, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/automotive-courses/">automotive courses</a>, and <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc30620-certificate-iii-in-painting-and-decorating/">painting and decorating courses in Sydney</a>.</p> <p>Students benefit from guidance provided by experienced trainers who understand industry expectations and help learners develop the skills employers value. Through practical training and professional support, we aim to help every student achieve their goals.</p> <h2><strong>Build Your Future with Skyline International College</strong></h2> <p>If you are ready to gain practical skills and enter one of Australia’s essential industries, our bricklaying course in Sydney could be the perfect starting point. Skyline International College is committed to helping students develop the knowledge, confidence, and hands-on experience needed for long-term success.</p> <p><a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/contact/">Contact our team today</a> to learn more about course availability, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/admissions-skyline-international-college/">admission requirements</a>, and enrolment opportunities.</p> </div>',
    total_course_duration = '52 Weeks (Includes term breaks)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 28000,
    enrolment_fee = 200,
    materials_fee = 2000,
    entry_requirements = '<div aria-expanded="true" class="w-tabs-section-content" id="content-1645787573297-1de0d9ea-2159" style=""><div class="w-tabs-section-content-h i-cf"><div class="wpb_text_column taab active"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><p>Skyline International College (SIC) follows the CPC Construction, Plumbing and Services Training Package guidance for the entry requirements for this qualification. There are no entry requirements for this qualification and direct entry is accepted.</p> <h4>Age and Academic Requirements:</h4> <p>International students must be 17 years or older and minimum completion of Australian Year 12 secondary school education equivalent or above.</p> <h4>English Language Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li>Academic IELTS 6.0 overall, no less than 5.5 in each band, upper intermediate, or EAP from an approved ELICOS/ESL center.</li> <li>Any AQF qualification at the Certificate III level or above in any discipline area delivered and assessed in English only will be deemed as meeting both the academic and English language entry requirements.</li> <li>Successfully complete the Language, Literacy, and Numeracy (LLN) and Digital literacy assessment provided by SIC prior to finalization of enrolment.</li> </ul> <h4>Physical requirements:</h4> <p>Participants of this course must have the ability to carry out workshop training involving physical activity, including lifting. A desire to work in a variety of indoor and outdoor environments is a key to work as a Bricklayer or Blocklayer or Paver.</p> </div></div></div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc33020-certificate-iii-in-bricklaying-and-blocklaying/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '120610J';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="wpb_wrapper"><h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Diploma of Building &amp; Construction Management Courses by Skyline International College</strong></h1> <p>Looking to move from hands-on construction into a leadership role? The Diploma of Building and Construction at <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/">Skyline International College</a> equips you with the knowledge, tools, and real-world confidence to manage building projects across the residential and commercial sectors. Whether you’re already on the tools or aiming to enter construction management, this course helps you step up, with recognised training and trusted guidance.</p> <p>Skyline is one of Sydney’s most practical, industry-attuned training providers. Our reputation is built on preparing future professionals who can lead, not just follow, on construction sites. With strong industry links, supportive trainers, and a practical learning model, this course puts you in control of your career progression.</p> <p>Skyline International College is known for delivering career-focused building and construction courses near Sydney that reflect how real construction sites operate, not just how textbooks describe them.</p> <section class="mbr-section courses-section"> <div class="lw_col-inner"> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>CPC50220 Diploma of Building and Construction (Building)</strong></h2> <p>This qualification reflects the role of building professionals who apply knowledge of structural principles, risk and financial management, estimating, preparing and administering building and construction contracts, selecting contractors, overseeing the work and its quality and managing construction work in building projects, including residential and commercial, with the following limitations:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Residential construction limited to National Construction Code Class 1 and 10 buildings to a maximum of 3 storeys.</li> <li>Commercial construction limited to National Construction Code Class 2 to 9 buildings, Type C and B construction.</li> </ul> <p>The construction industry strongly affirms that training and assessment leading to recognition of skills must be undertaken in a real or very closely simulated workplace environment. To achieve this qualification, the candidate must have access to a live building and construction workplace to meet the requirements detailed in the Assessment Requirements of core unit CPCCBC4008 Supervise communication and administration processes for building and construction projects.</p> <p>Completion of the general construction induction training program specified by the model Code of Practice for Construction Work is required for any person who is to carry out construction work. Achievement of unit CPCCWHS1001 Prepare to work safely in the construction industry meets this requirement.</p> <p>Builder licensing varies across States and Territories, and requirements additional to the attainment of this qualification may be required.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Who This Course Is Designed For</strong></h2> <p>This qualification is ideal for:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Site supervisors or tradespeople looking to gain formal credentials</li> <li>Builders ready to move into project management or contract administration</li> <li>International students seeking hands-on, CRICOS-listed construction management courses</li> <li>Individuals aiming to meet part of the licensing requirements for builder registration</li> </ul> <p>If you’re ready to manage teams, budgets, schedules, and compliance, all while staying aligned with Australian building codes, this course gives you the foundation to do it with confidence.</p> <p><img alt="Course Image" class="title-img" decoding="async" src="https://sic.edu.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/building.jpg"/></p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>What You’ll Learn</strong></h2> <p>The diploma of building and construction prepares you to coordinate every phase of a project, from early estimates to final handover. The course is structured around real-world building scenarios and includes:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Structural principles and building regulations</li> <li>Cost estimating, budgeting, and procurement</li> <li>Managing subcontractors and selecting contractors</li> <li>Quality assurance and site inspections</li> <li>Legal contracts and tender documentation</li> <li>Workplace safety planning and incident prevention</li> <li>Team leadership and client communication</li> </ul> <p>To complete the course, you’ll need access to a live or closely simulated building site, especially for the unit CPCCBC4008, which focuses on supervising communication and administration in construction. You’ll also complete CPCCWHS1001 to meet White Card requirements for on-site work.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Where This Qualification Can Take You</strong></h2> <p>Once completed, this course opens doors to roles such as:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Site Supervisor</li> <li>Construction Project Manager</li> <li>Contract Administrator</li> <li>Building Estimator</li> <li>Licensed Builder (with additional state-specific licensing requirements)</li> </ul> <p>You’ll be qualified to manage residential buildings (Class 1 and 10) up to three storeys, and commercial buildings (Class 2 to 9) under Type B and C construction. Graduates of Skyline’s building and construction courses near Sydney are well positioned for both private and commercial projects across Australia. Whether you’re working on private housing or public infrastructure, your job options expand significantly with this credential under your belt.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Why Train with Skyline International College?</strong></h2> <p>Skyline is not just a training provider, it’s a launchpad for serious professionals. With our Sydney-based campus, expert trainers, and hands-on learning environments, we deliver far more than theory. Our approach blends structure with flexibility, so you can keep working while upskilling.</p> <p>We bring:</p> <ul class="catpara"> <li>Strong ties with construction employers</li> <li>Trainers with real building site experience</li> <li>Support for international and domestic students</li> <li>Simulated and live site-based assessments</li> <li>Clear pathways to builder licensing</li> </ul> <p>Our construction management courses focus on preparing you to lead, make decisions, and take full responsibility for successful site delivery. And our approach ensures students completing our building and construction courses near Sydney are job-ready, confident, and capable of leading from day one.</p> <h2 style="font-size: 2.5rem;"><strong>Ready to Take Charge of Your Future?</strong></h2> <p>If you’re serious about moving into a supervisory or management role in the construction sector, the Diploma of Building and Construction from Skyline International College offers a proven path. You can check for other courses as well, such as <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc30220-certificate-iii-in-carpentry/">carpentry</a>, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/hospitality-courses/">hospitality</a> and <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/automotive-courses/">mechanic courses</a>.</p> <p><a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/contact/">Get in touch today</a> to discuss your eligibility, <a data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://sic.edu.au/courses/">course schedule</a>, and following intake dates. The site won’t manage itself; be the one who leads it.</p> </div> </section> </div>',
    total_course_duration = '78 Weeks(Includes term breaks)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 22500,
    enrolment_fee = 200,
    materials_fee = 1500,
    entry_requirements = '<div aria-expanded="true" class="w-tabs-section-content" id="content-1645787573297-1de0d9ea-2159" style=""><div class="w-tabs-section-content-h i-cf"><div class="wpb_text_column taab active"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><p>Skyline International College (SIC) follows the CPC Construction, Plumbing and Services Training Package guidance for the entry requirements for this qualification. There are no entry requirements for this qualification and direct entry is accepted.</p> <h4>Academic Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li>Minimum completion of Australian Year 12 secondary school education equivalent or above.</li> </ul> <h4>English Language Requirements:</h4> <ul> <li> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify;"><span class="agcmg">Academic IELTS 6.0 overall, with no less than 5.5 in each band or Upper Intermediate or EAP completion from an approved ELICOS/ESL centre Or Equivalent English Test (e.g. PTE, TOEFL).</span></p> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify; color: rgba(35,31,32,var(--o42jjq,1)); caret-color: #231f20; --8sd0kg: none; --cyv3zq: 12px; --gjplxq: 1.985; --s8nbea: p;"><span style="color: rgba(35,31,32,var(--o42jjq,1)); caret-color: #231f20; --ys-xuq: none; font-kerning: none;"><span class="agcmg">An AQF qualification at Certificate III level or above in any discipline,</span> delivered and assessed in English, will also satisfy both academic and</span> English requirements.</p> <p class="cvgsua" style="text-align: justify;"><span class="agcmg">Successfully complete the Language, Literacy, and Numeracy (LLN) and Digital literacy assessment provided by SIC prior to finalization of enrolment.</span></p> </li> </ul> </div></div></div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://sic.edu.au/course/cpc50220-diploma-of-building-and-construction-building/',
    updated_at = NOW()
